spoint BILLBOARDS/IMPOSTORS NOT VISIBLE - root cause CONFIRMED live (browser inspection). The impostor far-LOD (Vegetation.js branch.addLOD(PlaneGeometry, createOctahedralImpostorMaterial(...), D3)) is wired correctly (4th LOD level, isImpostor:true, atlas baked map 1024px, impostorTransform scale ~111 matching the tree geometry). BUT the vendored @three.ez/octahedral-impostor vertex shader (client/vendor/octahedral-impostor/index.js, octahedral_impostor_shader_vertex) computes the billboard world position from a SINGLE `impostorTransform` mat4 UNIFORM - it does NOT read InstancedMesh2's per-instance matrix (matricesTexture / gl_InstanceID via USE_INSTANCING_INDIRECT). So ALL N impostor instances render STACKED at the same point (the single impostorTransform translation ~[-1,53,4]) instead of at each tree's position -> a single overlapping clump near origin, invisible from gameplay. The material was written for a SINGLE OctahedralImpostor Mesh (one tree), incompatible with InstancedMesh2 instancing out of the box. FIX (= the shared-atlas VegImpostorTier work): FORK the impostor vertex shader so the billboard center+scale come from the per-instance instanceMatrix (the lib already injects USE_INSTANCING_INDIRECT + matricesTexture; the impostor's project_vertex replacement must use the instanced model matrix, not impostorTransform, for placement - keep impostorTransform only for the local billboard quad scale relative to the instance). ALSO OBSERVED: ez-tree geometry is ~100 UNITS TALL (branchBox maxY 96.7, leafBox maxY 102; bounding sphere r~50-55) while placement scale is ~0.75-1.25 and LOD cutover distances are D1=14 D2=35 D3=96 'metres' - a 100-unit tree vs 14m LOD0 distance is a scale mismatch (trees switch LOD/impostor almost immediately relative to their size); worth normalizing tree native scale OR expressing LOD distances in tree-heights. Witnessed via window.__veg._meshes[0].branch.LODinfo.objects[3].material.ezImpostorUniforms.impostorTransform + geometry.boundingSphere.